{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Draw near to the altar</b> — two tags on the resh, for Aaron was ashamed, and Moses said to him: Fortunate are you that you are chosen and draw near — \"draw near,\" for in you did YHWH choose. And furthermore, the altar appeared to him like the horns of an ox on account of the sin of the calf." "<b>And atone</b> — three times: here, and the other וכפר על העם regarding the incense, and וכפר על חטאתינו. To teach: just as a sacrifice atones for sin, so too the incense atones for sin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:03.372021535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}